p1 = {name:"Basic", attributes:["1 vCPU","1 GB RAM","25 GB SSD","1 TB bandwidth","1 IPv4","$5/mo"]}
p2 = {name:"Pro", attributes:["2 vCPU","4 GB RAM","50 GB SSD","2 TB bandwidth","1 IPv4","$15/mo"]}
p3 = {name:"Team", attributes:["4 vCPU","8 GB RAM","100 GB SSD","4 TB bandwidth","1 IPv4","$30/mo"]}
:::

The **Pro** plan is the best balance of price and resources for most workloads — it offers a big step up in RAM and bandwidth over Basic at a reasonable cost. The **Basic** plan is sufficient for small static sites or lightweight API servers, while **Team** makes sense once you need to run multiple services or heavier databases.

